{# narrative_engine/plot_verb — which step comes next in a scheme.
   Asked once per position by PlotPlanning::Plan until the model answers
   done or the plan reaches its cap. The answer is a verb id, or done.
   Receives: mastermind { name, standing }, bio { summary, occupation, ... },
     ambition, scheme, steps [string] (numbered, with how each went if it
     has happened), options [{ key, line }].
   NOTE: no fenced blocks and no literal braces anywhere in this file. #}
[ state who ]
{{ mastermind.name }}{% if length(mastermind.standing) > 0 %}, {{ mastermind.standing }}{% endif %}.
{{ bio.summary }}
{{ bio.occupation }}
[ end state ]

[ state aims ]
What they are ultimately after: {{ ambition }}
The scheme they have started, which these steps must accomplish: {{ scheme }}
[ end state ]

[ state plan ]
{% if length(steps) == 0 %}No steps have been chosen yet.{% else %}{% for s in steps %}{{ s }}
{% endfor %}{% endif %}
[ end state ]

[ question verb choice ]
What should `who` do next to bring about the scheme in `aims`, given the steps already in `plan`? Each step should build on the one before it, and the last step chosen should be the one that accomplishes the scheme. Choose the kind of step that fits this person and this scheme; who or what it involves is decided afterwards.
[ criteria ]
{% for o in options %}{{ o.key }}: {{ o.line }}
{% endfor %}[ end criteria ]
[ end question ]
